# DNA-AND content · life · protists (domain Eukaryotes, the single-celled and simple complex life)
# researched: Lumen / OpenStax Biology "Groups of Protists" (supergroups Excavata, SAR, Archaeplastida,
#   Amoebozoa, Opisthokonta); CUNY open biology text
# Note: protists are a grab-bag, not one true branch; their grouping is still changing in science.
# Spec: docs/CONTENT-FORMAT.md · wiki/systems/r08-life-sim.md

# ── Supergroups ──

@supergroup excavata
name: Excavates
real: yes
says: single cells, many with a feeding groove and several whip tails
members: euglenids, trypanosomes, diplomonads (Giardia), parabasalids

@supergroup sar
name: SAR (stramenopiles, alveolates, rhizarians)
real: yes
says: a huge group: diatoms, brown algae, dinoflagellates, ciliates, the malaria parasite, forams and radiolarians

@supergroup archaeplastida
name: Archaeplastids
real: yes
says: life with the first captured chloroplasts: red algae, green algae, and the land plants that grew from them

@supergroup amoebozoa
name: Amoebozoans
real: yes
says: amoebas and slime molds that crawl with blunt finger-like arms

@supergroup opisthokonta
name: Opisthokonts
real: yes
says: life with a single tail at the back: choanoflagellates, and the fungi and animals that grew from this line

# ── Protist groups (seeds) ──

@protist euglena
name: Euglenids
real: yes
supergroup: excavata
says: green swimmers that can both make food from light and eat

@protist trypanosome
name: Trypanosomes
real: yes
supergroup: excavata
says: parasites carried by insects

@protist diatom
name: Diatoms
real: yes
supergroup: sar
says: drifters in glass shells; make a large share of the oxygen in the seas

@protist brown-algae
name: Brown algae
real: yes
supergroup: sar
says: kelp and big seaweeds

@protist golden-algae
name: Golden algae
real: yes
supergroup: sar

@protist water-mold
name: Water molds
real: yes
supergroup: sar
says: fungus-like rotters of plants and fish

@protist dinoflagellate
name: Dinoflagellates
real: yes
supergroup: sar
says: spinning swimmers; some glow, some cause poisonous red tides

@protist ciliate
name: Ciliates
real: yes
supergroup: sar
says: covered in rows of beating hairs
example: Paramecium

@protist apicomplexan
name: Apicomplexans
real: yes
supergroup: sar
says: parasites that pierce cells
example: the malaria parasite

@protist foram
name: Forams
real: yes
supergroup: sar
says: tiny shells of chalk that build up into rock over ages

@protist radiolarian
name: Radiolarians
real: yes
supergroup: sar
says: ornate glass skeletons with thin threadlike arms

@protist red-algae
name: Red algae
real: yes
supergroup: archaeplastida
says: seaweeds that grow in deep water

@protist green-algae
name: Green algae
real: yes
supergroup: archaeplastida
says: the ancestors of land plants

@protist amoeba
name: Amoebas
real: yes
supergroup: amoebozoa
says: shape-shifting hunters that crawl and engulf food

@protist slime-mold
name: Slime molds
real: yes
supergroup: amoebozoa
says: single cells that gather into a crawling body; can solve mazes without a brain

@protist choanoflagellate
name: Choanoflagellates
real: yes
supergroup: opisthokonta
says: collared cells, the closest living relatives of animals

# ── How they move ──

@move flagella
name: Whip tails (flagella)
real: yes

@move cilia
name: Beating hairs (cilia)
real: yes

@move pseudopodia
name: Crawling arms (pseudopodia)
real: yes

@move drifting
name: Drifting
real: yes
says: floating with the current

# ── Generator rules ──

@rule protist-complex
real: rule
says: protists are the first complex cells, with a nucleus and parts inside; they appear after the swallowed-partners stage

@rule protist-roots
real: rule
says: protist lines lead on: green algae to land plants, choanoflagellate-like cells to animals, opisthokont cells to fungi

@rule protist-food
real: rule
says: drifting protists are the base of the sea's food chain; their blooms feed everything, and some blooms poison it

@rule protist-rock
real: rule
says: chalk and glass shells of dead protists pile up into rock on the sea floor
